# System

**Color:** `#636E72` | **Nodes:** 5

The System category provides nodes that interact with the operating system and runtime environment.

## Info

### Current Time

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `system/info/currentTime` |
| **Node Name** | Current Time |
| **Description** | Outputs the current system time as a formatted string and a numeric Unix timestamp. No inputs required. |

**Inputs** — none

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `time` | String | Formatted time string (e.g., `"2026-05-11 14:30:00"`) |
| `timestamp` | Float | Unix timestamp in seconds since epoch |

**Example Usage**

```
[Current Time] → [Number Display]  (timestamp)
             → [Text Display]      (formatted time)
```

### Environment Variable

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `system/info/envVar` |
| **Node Name** | Environment Variable |
| **Description** | Reads the value of a system environment variable by name. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `name` | String | `""` | Name of the environment variable (e.g., `"HOME"`, `"PATH"`) |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `value` | String | Value of the environment variable, or empty if not found |

### OS Info

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `system/info/osInfo` |
| **Node Name** | OS Info |
| **Description** | Reports the operating system name, kernel version, and architecture. No inputs required. |

**Inputs** — none

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `os` | String | OS name (e.g., `"Linux"`, `"Windows"`, `"macOS"`) |
| `kernel` | String | Kernel version string |
| `architecture` | String | CPU architecture (e.g., `"x86_64"`, `"arm64"`) |

## I/O

### Clipboard

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `system/io/clipboard` |
| **Node Name** | Clipboard |
| **Description** | Reads or writes the system clipboard. Set `set` to `true` to write the provided `text`. Reads clipboard contents when `set` is `false`. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `text` | String | `""` | Text to write to clipboard when `set` is true |
| `set` | Bool | `false` | If true, writes `text` to clipboard; if false, reads clipboard |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `text` | String | Current clipboard contents |

## Process

### Process Execute

| | |
|---|---|
| **Type** | `system/process/execute` |
| **Node Name** | Process Execute |
| **Description** | Executes a system command and captures its output. Useful for running shell commands, scripts, or other programs from within the graph. |

**Inputs**

| Port | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `command` | String | `""` | Command to execute (e.g., `"ls -la"`, `"echo hello"`) |

**Outputs**

| Port | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `output` | String | Standard output from the command |
| `success` | Bool | Whether the command exited successfully (exit code 0) |
